This line in your TResBlock:

h .+= reshape(m.emb_proj(t_emb), 1, 1, size(h,3), size(h,4))

does an in-place mutation (.+=) on h.
💥 Why is this bad for Zygote?

Zygote does not support in-place mutations like .+=, .=, copyto!, etc., because it relies on immutable data flow to track gradients.
✅ How to fix it

Instead of

h .+= something

Write

h = h .+ something

💡 Your corrected TResBlock forward function

function (m::TResBlock)(x, t_emb)
    h = gelu.(m.conv1(x))
    # broadcast time embedding to (1,1,C,B) and add
    h = h .+ reshape(m.emb_proj(t_emb), 1, 1, size(h,3), size(h,4))
    h = gelu.(m.conv2(h))
    return h .+ (m.skip === identity ? x : m.skip(x))
end

✅ Explanation

    h = h .+ something makes a new array rather than modifying in place.

    Zygote can now correctly build the computational graph.

